# Default registry stays registry.npmjs.org ON PURPOSE.
#
# Packages in this repo publish to PUBLIC npm so esm.sh can serve them. esm.sh is a
# proxy over registry.npmjs.org and cannot authenticate to a private registry, so a
# package that lands on npm.ch5.me is invisible to it — forever, and silently.
#
# That is not hypothetical. `hush/.npmrc` maps `@chriscode:registry=https://npm.ch5.me/`
# and `hush-cli/package.json` sets `publishConfig.registry` to the same. Result:
# public npm still serves @chriscode/hush@7.5.0 while the repo is on 8.3.1, and
# esm.sh has been pinned three majors back with every publish reporting success.
#
# So: do NOT add a @chriscode registry line here, and do NOT put `registry` inside
# any publishConfig in packages/*. `scripts/verify-esm.ts` checks for the drift.
@ch5me:registry=https://npm.ch5.me/
//npm.ch5.me/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}
